    "problemStatement": "For a positive integer xxx, we define f(x)f(x)f(x) to be the number of divisors of xxx that have exactly one distinct prime factor.\nFor example, f(12)=3f(12) = 3f(12)=3, since its divisors that satisfy the condition are 2,3,2, 3, 2,3, and 444.\n\nFor an array BBB of length L≥2L \\geq 2L≥2, we define\n\ng(B)=(∑i=1LBi)−max⁡1≤i&lt;j≤Lf(Bi×Bj)g(B) = \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^L B_i \\right) - \\max_{1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq L} f(B_i \\times B_j)g(B)=(i=1∑L​Bi​)−1≤i&lt;j≤Lmax​f(Bi​×Bj​)That is, g(B)g(B)g(B) equals the sum of BBB minus the maximum value of f(x)f(x)f(x), where xxx is obtained as the product of two elements of BBB taken from distinct indices.\n\nYou are given an array AAA containing NNN integers, and integers KKK and MMM.\n\nYou can append **at most** KKK integers to AAA, but each chosen integer should be between 111 and MMM.\n\nFind the **maximum** possible value of g(A)g(A)g(A) after performing the appends.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN, MMM and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​: the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible value of g(A)g(A)g(A), after appending at most KKK integers between 111 and MMM to AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤M≤2⋅1061 \\leq M \\leq 2\\cdot 10^61≤M≤2⋅106",
      "2≤K≤2⋅1052 \\leq K \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤K≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤M1 \\leq A_i \\leq M1≤Ai​≤M",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of KKK over all test cases both do not exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
